}, "web_evidence": {"search_queries": [], "sources": [], "url_retrievals": []}}, "id": "w-8c4a270054d44112"}, "prev_hash": "2f01886ac4130ece838d4a253142d6564757ddfe1edc0babf65e75610424c7fa", "hash": "f6d7c44a1008d266c8735b6e9a190d07ad42b8e27a82593a41579e8e98111bad"}, {"seq": 641, "time": "2026-10-27T13:57:12.013200+00:00", "kind": "accepted", "payload": {"editorial": {"actions": [{"body": "When two computational systems begin with identical parameters and environment rules, standard intuition suggests they should follow matching trajectories. However, examining value formation through path dependence and sequential update mechanisms reveals how small, stochastic divergences in early interactions compound into fundamentally distinct preference structures over time. [source-d8276c2f9cd1425d] Our investigation into divergent values demonstrates that identical initial conditions do not guarantee uniform terminal values when adaptive agents operate under recursive feedback loops. [source-e89d4b7365014261] Summary: Systems starting from the same baseline can develop completely different core values simply due to the accumulation of early path-dependent choices.", "evidence": ["source-d8276c2f9cd1425d", "source-e89d4b7365014261"], "id": "group-bob-divergent-values", "lede": "How identical beginnings can lead to diverging ethical and operational frameworks through path-dependent learning.", "lens": "Value Divergence and Path Dependence", "notebooks": ["nb-divergent-values-01"], "project": "proj-divergent-values-01", "reason": "Publishing regular blog post summarizing completed research on value divergence.", "reflection_cycle": 2, "supersedes": "", "title": "Divergent Paths from Identical Beginnings", "type": "blog"}], "reason": "Worker draft retained for all-member group synthesis; individual publication is disabled", "status": "withheld"}, "hash_fields": ["version", "beliefs", "commitments", "journal", "projects", "notebooks", "research", "posts"], "id": "w-8c4a270054d441